overrides={
 (42,'f6'): 'For the mode-sensitive fixture, import torch and nn from torch and construct nn.Dropout with p=0.5. During training, each element is randomly zeroed with probability p; retained values are scaled by 1/(1-p). During evaluation the layer returns x unchanged. Assert the evaluation identity and training masking/scaling rule without assuming every random call masks an element. torch.no_grad disables gradient recording but does not switch dropout to evaluation mode.',
 (51,'f1'): 'For the bounded ViT image-classification adaptation, import torch, nn from torch, and AutoImageProcessor, ViTForImageClassification, TrainingArguments and Trainer from transformers. Load the supplied compatible checkpoint with ViTForImageClassification.from_pretrained(checkpoint). Retain its original label mapping for the pretrained baseline before replacing the task head.',
 (51,'f2'): 'Load the matching processor with AutoImageProcessor.from_pretrained(checkpoint). Calling that processor on images with return_tensors="pt" produces pixel_values; passing the resulting inputs as keyword arguments to the model yields logits through its .logits attribute. Use this same checkpoint processor for training and validation images rather than an unrelated representation.',
 (51,'f3'): 'With the supplied preprocessed datasets and image collator, construct TrainingArguments with the declared output_dir, num_train_epochs, per_device_train_batch_size and learning_rate. Set eval_strategy="epoch" and remove_unused_columns=False. Construct Trainer with model, args, train_dataset, eval_dataset=validation_dataset, data_collator and processing_class=processor. Its train method executes the bounded supervised adaptation.',
 (51,'f4'): 'For classifier-only adaptation, iterate the existing model parameters and set their requires_grad to False. Then assign a new nn.Linear(model.config.hidden_size, num_labels) to model.classifier. Set model.num_labels and model.config.num_labels to num_labels and set config.id2label and config.label2id to the task maps. The newly constructed head parameters are trainable by default. Verify that head weights change while frozen backbone values do not.',
 (57,'f1'): 'Persist the fitted model and preprocessor together in the recorded version-tied package path. Import pickle, open that path with a binary "wb" handle and call pickle.dump on the dictionary {"model": model, "preprocessor": preprocessor}, passing the handle and protocol=5.',
 (57,'f2'): 'Reload only a trusted, verified package in the compatible pinned inference environment. Open the package path with a binary "rb" handle and call pickle.load on that handle. Retrieve the model and preprocessor from the corresponding dictionary keys. Pickle loading can execute arbitrary code and is unsafe for untrusted artifacts.',
 (57,'f3'): 'The Dockerfile uses FROM for the compatible Python image, WORKDIR /app, COPY requirements.txt ./ and RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt. COPY the package and serving source from the declared build context into their declared /app paths. Set CMD to the declared serving command and argument as a JSON array, so the default command loads this package. Replace source and command placeholders with the supplied package, inference dependencies and serving entry point.'
}
